file: "packages/editor/src/shell/palette_items.ts"
doc: "Builders turning commands and scene elements into palette rows."

methods: [
  { name: "commandPaletteItems"
    change_type: MODIFIED
    doc:
      "The filter changes source. It stops consulting PALETTE_EXCLUDED, which\n"
      "is deleted with its module, and reads command.appliesTo instead: a\n"
      "command is offered when appliesTo is present, and skipped when it is\n"
      "absent. Everything else -- the row shape, the chord lookup, the\n"
      "`command:` key prefix, the order -- is unchanged.\n"
      "\n"
      "The palette does NOT apply the kind-list part of the rule. It is\n"
      "reached from a chord with no pointer context and is a search over\n"
      "everything the editor can do, so an element-specific command stays\n"
      "listed whatever the selection; running it with a selection it does not\n"
      "suit is already a no-op in its own body. Only the context menu filters\n"
      "by selection, because only it is opened AT something.\n"
      "\n"
      "PALETTE_EXCLUDED held exactly eleven ids: 'escape', the four nudges,\n"
      "'ring-next', 'ring-prev', 'open-palette', 'open-help', 'enter-grab'\n"
      "and 'enter-resize'. Nine of those eleven are exactly the commands that\n"
      "get no appliesTo, so the new rule excludes them for the same effect by\n"
      "a different route. That leaves two, both 'global':\n"
      "\n"
      "  'open-palette'  STILL EXCLUDED, by a single explicit id check in\n"
      "                  this function. A palette row that reopens the\n"
      "                  palette you are already inside is a dead row.\n"
      "  'open-help'     NOW LISTED, which is a deliberate change. There is\n"
      "                  nothing self-referential about reaching the help\n"
      "                  sheet from the palette, and 'Keyboard Shortcuts' is\n"
      "                  a row people look for.\n"
      "\n"
      "One id, not a set, and that is the whole of the reinstated exclusion.\n"
      "The objection to PALETTE_EXCLUDED was that an exclusion list grows\n"
      "silently stale as commands are added; a single literal guarding a\n"
      "single self-reference does not have that shape, because the only way\n"
      "to need a second entry is to add a second command that opens the\n"
      "palette. It stays local rather than becoming a Command field because\n"
      "it is self-reference, not applicability -- the context menu should\n"
      "offer 'open-palette' quite happily."
    inputs: [
      { name: "commands", type: { named: { symbol: "ReadonlyArray", args: [{ named: { symbol: "Command" } }] } } },
      { name: "keymap",   type: { named: { symbol: "ReadonlyArray", args: [{ named: { symbol: "KeymapEntry" } }] } } }
    ]
    output: { named: { symbol: "Array", args: [{ named: { symbol: "PaletteItem" } }] } }
    uses: ["formatChord"]
  }
]
